<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hendrick Theyanoguin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1691–<a href="/years/1755">1755</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as King Hendrick, Tiyanoga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hendrick Theyanoguin was a Mohawk leader and one of the most influential Haudenosaunee spokesmen of his time, a close ally of the British and of William Johnson. He spoke forcefully at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albany-congress">Albany Congress</a> of 1754 about British neglect of the alliance. He was killed in 1755 leading Mohawk warriors for the British at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lake-george">Battle of Lake George</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hendrick-theyanoguin.jpg" alt="Hendrick Theyanoguin" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Engraver unknown, based on a lost portrait by an unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hendrick_Theyanoguin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
